  {
   "id": "s04",
   "text": {
    "en": "The first time it happened, I thought I was dreaming. I told my little brother, Leo. He just looked at me, smiled, and said I was being weird. The second time, I told my mom. By the tenth time, I stopped telling anyone. And honestly, at first, it was kind of fun. No homework mattered. No test counted. I could do whatever I wanted. But by loop fifty, it wasn't fun anymore."
