   "id": "s13",
   "text": {
    "en": "So at two fifty, I climbed the clock tower again. This time, I looked carefully. There were tiny footprints in the dust. Kid-sized footprints. And at the top, next to the big gear, someone had scratched lines into the wall. Hundreds of them. One for every day. I counted them. Four hundred and twelve."
